# Mana Flare: "Whenever a player taps a land for mana, that player adds one mana of any type that land produced" (CR
# 106.12a, 605.1b). Turn 2: Bot2's Forest taps for {G}{G} into Bot2's own pool ("that player"; Bot1's stays empty), and Bot2
# casts Llanowar Elves with it. Turn 4: the Elves, a creature and no land, tap for {G} alone. Turn 5: Bot1's Azorius
# Chancery produces {W}{U}, two types, so Bot1 chooses one ("If you tap a land for more than one mana, you choose one type
# that was produced", its ruling): {U}, for {W}{U}{U}; one type, not both (`! Bot1.Modes(1; 2)`). The Mountain tapped on
# turn 1 before the Flare was out gave {R} alone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Mana Flare
Azorius Chancery
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Mana Flare.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
? Bot2.Mana = {G}{G}
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
